{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6192bf8302a20700d883f8e27bea46437d6551e0edf9af2f3e111980a50fd0aa","digest":{"component_or_area":"operation-scoped configuration and provider-auth composition","key_entities":["OperationSnapshot","REBAR_ROOT","REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH","REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","PydanticAIRunner","ProviderSession","GitRuntime","LLMRuntime","BridgeRuntime","SecretStr","SecretBytes","check_config_reads.py","ADR 0098","RP-01","resolve_with_sources"],"problem_keywords":["configuration resolution","provider authentication","credential composition","operation scope","immutability","ambient state"],"propositions":["Configuration must resolve once per operation boundary with precedence: explicit input > environment > project config > user config > schema default, producing an immutable, serializable, non-secret OperationSnapshot.","Authentication across LLM, Git, bridge, MCP, review-bot, and op-cert must compose consistently without rereading ambient state mid-operation or falling back to unintended principals.","Runtime bindings (GitRuntime, LLMRuntime, BridgeRuntime) must own credential lifecycles; Rebar factories retain only transport/output policy and inject auth only through RP-01's ProviderSession path.","Op-cert must accept exactly one of REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH or REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY, validate before service work, copy into a process-owned 0700/0600 file, and fail closed on invalid composition.","An AST ownership gate must derive config/credential names from authoritative registries, reject direct/aliased reads below approved seams, permit only exact path/symbol+rationale exceptions, and reach zero legacy exceptions at cutover.","All affected CLI, library, MCP, reconciler, and hosted consumers must receive equivalent non-secret behavior from the approved precedence contract; captured operations must remain stable across environment/file/cwd mutation."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787171637649486001,"uuid":"e2ac4af3-5ddb-4ca3-ac4f-a07f7528d567"}